        "content": "<p>Takashiidobe opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14699\">issue #14699</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h4>Feature</h4>\n<p>Optimization of unsigned constant-remainder tests:</p>\n<p>Take a look at: <a href=\"https://godbolt.org/z/MPfdhbc3q\">https://godbolt.org/z/MPfdhbc3q</a> (divide x by constant, in this case 7, and then test it). </p>\n<p>for signed/unsigned x, and for == and !=, rustc on llvm emits a short sequence, e.g. for the != case</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"GAS\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nl\">is_multiple_of_7:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nf\">imul</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">edi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">-1227133513</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nf\">cmp</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">613566757</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nf\">setae</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"no\">al</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nf\">ret</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The corresponding cranelift side is much longer:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"GAS\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nl\">is_multiple_of_7:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">rax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rdi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">mul</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">dword</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">ptr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"no\">rip</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0x2b</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\"># 0x38 &lt;is_multiple_of_7+0x38&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">r10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rdi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">sub</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">r10d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">edx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">shr</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">r10d</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">add</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">r10d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">edx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">shr</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">r10d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0x2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">imul</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"no\">r11d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">r10d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0x7</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">sub</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"no\">edi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">r11d</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">test</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"no\">edi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">edi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">setne</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"no\">al</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"nf\">movzx</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"no\">rax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">al</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h4>Benefit</h4>\n<p>llvm-mca says this is 8 cycles for llvm or 20 for cranelift on a zen4. There is a similar disparity for arm64 and riscv64. </p>\n<h4>Implementation</h4>\n<p>Not sure. LLVM implements this in target independent SDAG, maybe there's a similar target independent ISLE fold that would be a good place for it?</p>\n<p>extra note: make sure to handle signed vs unsigned, ne and eq, and odd and even numbers.</p>\n<h4>Alternatives</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>We could leave this as is. I think this is a mildly popular pattern, like for byte aligning so I'd like to see it improved.</li>\n<li>Would need to look into cranelift more for other places to put this optimization. It could be target dependent but I assume this optimization should work the same for any target since it's a strength reduction.<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
